[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Frozen corpus individual requested-analysis qualification

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This is an offline qualification coordinator over the existing public frontend/client, not a new production parser or simulator. Existing Simulator.Benchmarks.Tables reads named print tables, rejects negative/descending axes and is internal; it cannot retain full complex native RAW columns. A bounded ASCII RAW adapter is therefore confined to Simulator.RequestedQualification. No third-party dependency was added. Native format research: https://github.com/ngspice/ngspice/blob/master/src/frontend/rawfile.c (inspected 2026-11-02); exact executed native binary SHA256 is recorded per campaign. This does not qualify all RAW variants.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Original independent requested analyses
STATEMENT: >>>
The coordinator shall retain every frozen inventory identity and original analysis identity, resolve resources through the existing generated frontend, and execute only successfully prepared ordinary requested analyses. Native oracle jobs shall preserve expanded original physical cards and one original analysis card, masking other analyses and output/reporting cards by generated source ranges. Native jobs shall independently evaluate original arguments and parameters. Unmodeled input-control instructions and original shell/file actions shall never execute. Validated finite analysis controls may dispatch typed requests and individually scoped native projections under requested-control-profile.sdoc.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.RequestedQualification/RequestedCorpus.cs and QualificationSupport.cs; scripts/Run-RequestedCorpus.cs. Tests: RequestedQualificationTests.cs. Individual analysis projections and all omission ranges/hashes are retained. This is not complete input-control-program parity. Static selected OP preparation is reported only as a separate circuit-preparation stage and cannot count as requested execution.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Bounded complete-grid numerical evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
The coordinator shall enforce child deadlines, between-job admission budgets, bounded native RAW shapes, stable identities and SI units, finite values and complete original OP/DC/AC grids. It shall compare all mapped root voltages and supported root branch currents when available. Missing observables, native grid discrepancies and malformed results shall not count as numerical agreement. Transient reference interpolation shall not extrapolate or claim identical internal integration grids.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
RAW bounds:64MiB characters,2048variables,100000points,4000000complex cells. Native and engine children have30-second deadlines. Voltage/current absolute bounds are1e-6V/1e-9A plus1e-4relative; raw axis matching uses1e-12relative without a unit-sized absolute epsilon. These are qualification tolerances, not simulator accuracy guarantees.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Honest four-stage burndown and immutable source gate
STATEMENT: >>>
Reports and SVG shall distinguish syntax acceptance, circuit preparation, actual requested-analysis execution and actual native numerical agreement. Each stage shall retain measured successes, known refusals/failures and unknown/unattempted counts over the same inventory. A final source, assembly, executable, inventory and loaded-resource hash gate shall invalidate stage claims when provenance changes. Scheduled or partial campaigns shall not be reported as completed qualification.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No whole928-input campaign was run during coordinator implementation. Owned representative inputs verify refusal and agreement distinctions. Bulk artifacts remain outside Git; bounded evidence and commands are recorded in docs/requested-corpus-qualification.md and evidence/requested-corpus-coordinator.json.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Monotonic running progress durations
STATEMENT: >>>
Every running checkpoint shall report elapsed admission time from the same monotonic clock used by the final duration, without remaining zero until completion or regressing at the final checkpoint.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
RequestedProgressNativeTests observes real atomic checkpoints using FileSystemWatcher and a coalesced notification channel, checking positive running durations and nondecreasing elapsed values. Metadata acquisition/build time is outside the admission clock, preserving the final duration's existing scope. The older detached62ae97d census source is not modified retroactively.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-005
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Distinct-root blocker ranking without predicted unlock claims
STATEMENT: >>>
Offline prioritization shall require completed provenance-valid census evidence and a matching baseline inventory. It shall count distinct root identities separately from unique original content hashes, reject duplicate identities, retain overlapping diagnostic groups and distinguish reached primary refusals from bounded secondary structural observations. Sole observed issues and model-family presence shall not imply guaranteed executable or numerically agreeing circuits. Expanded inputs shall retain matching recorded hashes; unavailable, incomplete and truncated structural observations shall remain explicit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: CorpusBlockerRanking.cs and scripts/Rank-RequestedCorpus.cs reuse the generated parser and CircuitReadiness audit, without changing primary census outcomes. Verification: CorpusBlockerRankingTests exercises mirrors, repeated observations, duplicate refusal, intersections and 200 FsCheck order/multiplicity trials (replay 362,20261103). Current corpus report and scope-specific coverage/mutation evidence: docs/requested-corpus-fc5db25.md. This offline finite audit does not establish complete scalar, model or numerical validation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CAP-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-PZ-GROUNDED-RC-001
TITLE: Evaluate a first-order grounded RC voltage-transfer request
STATEMENT: >>>
The pole-zero frontend shall accept a single root .pz voltage-transfer directive for one ideal input voltage source, one series resistor and one grounded output capacitor. It shall publish the finite pole in inverse seconds for POL and PZ and an empty finite zero set. ZER shall return only the empty zero set. Unsupported ports, topologies, transfer modes, or additional analysis and control directives shall refuse without publishing roots.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: PoleZeroSelection and Run-PoleZero.cs. Verification: PoleZeroTests and the unmodified RSpice polezero/filt_rc.cir against ngspice. This entry point is separate from the general requested-analysis corpus coordinator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-PZ-BRIDGE-T-001
TITLE: Evaluate the real roots of a passive RC bridge-T
STATEMENT: >>>
The standalone pole-zero frontend shall admit a grounded voltage transfer with two capacitors in series from input to output, one grounded resistor at their common node, one bridging resistor from input to output, and one ideal input voltage source. It shall preserve repeated finite real roots in inverse seconds, honor POL, ZER and PZ selection, and refuse unsupported topology or root domain without publishing partial roots. It may select the requested .pz independently of an accompanying .op card.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: PoleZeroSelection. Verification: PoleZeroTests and the original RSpice polezero/filt_bridge_t.cir compared with an ngspice report projection retaining the original .pz and devices.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-PZ-CORPUS-DISPATCH-001
TITLE: Qualify bounded pole-zero analyses in the original corpus
STATEMENT: >>>
The corpus runner shall report the bounded root .pz and any accompanying .op as distinct operations. The native comparison shall preserve the original circuit and requested directive, isolate the selected analysis, validate plot identity and root multiplicity, and compare real roots in inverse seconds. Missing or unsupported roots shall not count as agreement.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RequestedCorpus and PoleZeroQualification. Verification: PoleZeroQualificationTests and the original RSpice filt_rc.cir and filt_bridge_t.cir requested-analysis replay.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CORPUS-PZ-CASCADE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact real poles of isolated RC and RL cascades
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded requested pole-zero profile shall evaluate grounded voltage-driven series-R shunt-C stages separated by unloaded ideal voltage-controlled voltage buffers, and grounded current-driven parallel-RL stages coupled by unilateral voltage-controlled current sources. Each cascade shall contain two to four stages. RC poles are -1/(RC) with no finite zeros, and the RL profile shall report poles only, at -R/L. Repeated roots shall retain multiplicity. Extra circuit elements, feedback, ambiguous stages, reused nodes and non-finite or nonnegative roots shall refuse the cascade factorization. An independent source with a bare AC clause shall use unit AC magnitude and zero phase, preserving any explicit DC bias.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: PoleZeroSelection, PoleZeroQualification and generated source-profile grammar. Verification: PoleZeroTests and SourceProfileTests, including repeated poles, loading and feedback refusal, bare AC with explicit DC before or after it, and malformed source tails. A reciprocal RL-pole mutant was detected. Qualification compares independently sorted ngspice real roots while retaining their counts and multiplicities.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Windows verification from 8ab09ee with this change, using RSpice corpus commit 29c28a022625fd7cc2c56ead1cce2d3066663074. Run scripts/Run-RequestedCorpus.cs with the checkout, RSpice tests/ngspice directory, native engine, ngspice console, inventory-final.json, fresh output directory and a 30-second admission budget. Original deck SHA-256 values: filt_multistage.cir 524cb091e3438801cec51b105dc16f3db6e07f9e973e9e4ace1e05d29aeeabb0; pz2.cir 603fb0764c82f15d3413cae549fadd883c317f0d24cc0639f310723259627a14; pzt.cir e8f9363c3cf02ee0637cb5525ae67f7edcab7256e1f9b1cac485633f92ddc71e. All three executed their original .pz and agreed with ngspice 47+ across all ten poles. The largest absolute discrepancy was 7.63e-6 per second on the 5e10 per second RC pole. Existing filt_rc.cir and filt_bridge_t.cir also retained full requested-analysis agreement. The managed factorization owns this selected analysis, so these results do not qualify a general native pole-zero solver.

The Frontend.Tests filter FullyQualifiedName~PoleZero|FullyQualifiedName~Source|FullyQualifiedName~RequestedQualification passed 113 cases with four environment-gated skips. Coverlet line/branch coverage was 97.45/80.69 percent for PoleZeroSelection, 73.07/67.24 percent for PoleZeroQualification, and 81.81/74.54 percent for SourceProfileExtraction. Native coverage and a dedicated fuzz campaign were outside this run. Artifacts, frozen inventory, and per-deck comparisons are under E:/Artifacts/Spice-pz-three-8ab09ee.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CORPUS-PZ-HIGHPASS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Passive two-port high-pass transimpedance roots
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded pole-zero profile shall accept a grounded current-driven transfer across two resistive shunts coupled only by one capacitor. It shall report the real pole at -1/(C*(Rin+Rout)) and the zero at the origin according to the requested pol, zer or pz mode. Both resistors and the coupling capacitor shall match the requested ports. Extra branches and nonrepresentable time constants shall refuse.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: PoleZeroSelection. Verification: PoleZeroTests uses unequal shunts and tests all three modes. A mutant omitting the output shunt failed both pole-bearing tests. The original RSpice polezero/simplepz.cir compared one pole and one zero with the unchanged ngspice circuit.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SOURCE-AC-ASSIGNMENT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit AC magnitude assignment
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated source profile shall accept AC=<magnitude> with the same phase and DC-bias semantics as AC <magnitude>. An equals sign without a magnitude shall refuse rather than select the bare AC default.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: SpiceParser.g4. Verification: SourceProfileTests and the original ac-zero.cir preparation comparison. Zero-frequency AC and that deck's control program remain separate requirements.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Windows baseline 4b20e13 and final replay used ten unchanged RSpice inputs from corpus commit 29c28a022625fd7cc2c56ead1cce2d3066663074. Inventory SHA-256 657B99CB6A61CB4ADC13A45FBEFF762D56B8A2FE051186532C506B5654854B05. Run scripts/Run-RequestedCorpus.cs with the checkout, corpus root, engine, ngspice 47+, frozen inventory, fresh output and 30-second admission budget. All ten originally refused preparation. The final run qualified simplepz.cir, SHA-256 cd6ccd81115df42624729b9842e8ff8363c56709cb8df813e3cd8afb0dd857dd, with pole -5e8 per second and zero at the origin. Native pole error was 1.79e-7 per second, within the 1e-7 absolute plus 1e-9 relative tolerance. The source profile of ac-zero.cir now binds. Its let expression and zero-frequency AC remain unqualified. The remaining eight decks still refused preparation. The final and baseline summaries and per-case diagnostics are under E:/Artifacts/Spice-ten-4b20e13.

The Frontend.Tests filter FullyQualifiedName~PoleZero|FullyQualifiedName~SourceProfileTests passed 41 cases without skips. Coverlet line/branch coverage was 96.15/80.90 percent for PoleZeroSelection and 76.36/62.72 percent for SourceProfileExtraction. Native coverage and dedicated fuzz and randomized campaigns were outside this replay.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CORPUS-AC-ZERO-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Zero-frequency incremental AC and bounded real reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
A requested linear AC sweep may begin at zero hertz. Decade and octave sweeps shall retain positive frequency bounds. The engine shall use the same incremental conductance and excitation phasors as at positive frequencies, with zero reactive stamps and verified residuals. Terminal real-vector reporting may consume a single zero-hertz result only when the result identity and axis match and all imaginary components are zero. Unspaced division immediately after a parenthesized expression shall remain an arithmetic operator in the bounded control lexer.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: native AC assembly, complex audit, legacy linear-grid importer, RequestedAnalysis and RequestedControlReporting, corpus axis checks and semantic control lexer. Tests: ZeroFrequencyAcTests covers generated control preparation, negative/logarithmic grids and refusal of a synthetic nonreal result. sparse_ac_circuits checks a complex input phasor through ideal L and C DC limits on LU and Faer.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Windows verification from deab565 with REQ-CORPUS-AC-ZERO-001. Replayed the same ten original inputs using Run-RequestedCorpus.cs and the previous pinned inventory, with a 30-second admission budget. Original ac-zero.cir SHA-256 0bf37dea1b53f5f79bb042038599fb6c19bd5dc50c18657e8bdc98fd43d194ef. New native engine SHA-256 4B283A871347AB56790E089E204F3D56D2F80F25281A664C3628DE2BD06DA81E. ngspice 47+ SHA-256 12BC57018AA5142D28065704D09BC6B06DA2A3886F7864CA042ED4824CCF910F. Its unchanged control program exited successfully. Our replay compared all five mapped observables at 0 Hz with maximum difference 1.09e-19 A and exact node-voltage agreement. Our terminal program reported INFO: success, err=0 and exit code 0. simplepz.cir retained agreement. Eight decks still refused preparation.

cargo test --locked -j 1 --test sparse_ac --test sparse_ac_circuits --test analysis_audits passed 27 tests, including the existing 32-case RC property with seed 2026103006. The Windows process-tree watchdog used an aggregate and per-tree limit of 850 MiB. Managed filters ZeroFrequencyAcTests, RequestedQualificationTests, SourceProfileTests and RequestedControl matched 90 passes and three environment-gated skips. Coverlet line/branch percentages were 90.24/55.88 for RequestedControlReporting.cs and 81.08/46.90 for RequestedComparison. A deliberate removal of the imaginary-component rejection failed its regression. Native coverage and a dedicated fuzz run were outside this checkpoint. Evidence is under E:/Artifacts/Spice-ac-zero-deab565.
<<<
